## License finding requiring release review

The binary NuGet packages `Json.More.Net@3.0.1`, `JsonPatch.Net@5.0.2` and
`JsonPointer.Net@7.0.1` contain an Open Source Maintenance Fee Agreement (OSMFEULA) in
addition to the upstream MIT source license. The agreement states that some users of the
project's precompiled binary releases in revenue-generating activities owe a maintenance fee.
These packages enter this repository only through `Aspire.Hosting@13.5.3` and are part of the
development AppHost dependency graph, not the bOps CLI/API runtime graph. Do not classify or
distribute those binary packages as plain MIT without reviewing the embedded agreement and the
intended commercial use. Upstream sources:

- https://github.com/json-everything/json-everything/blob/master/LICENSE
- https://github.com/json-everything/json-everything/blob/master/OSMFEULA.txt

